cl emits a scalar deleting destructor ??_GPlain@@QEAAPEAXI@Z for a non-polymorphic class it deletes and cxx1 emits none, calling the destructor and then operator delete in line instead - a difference in what code is generated rather than in what anything is called, which is the same reason destructor.nocl and cleanup.nocl record. The virtual half of this case does agree: ??_GPoly@@UEAAPEAXI@Z is emitted by both, and it is the one this case drives through a null pointer
